EIGHT TRIGRAMS SEAL — FUINJUTSU REFERENCE
Konohagakure Sealing Archive — Jonin+ / Sealing Corps

The Eight Trigrams Sealing Style is a powerful fuinjutsu used to contain
tailed-beast chakra within a jinchuriki. It was employed by the Fourth
Hokage, Minato Namikaze, to seal the Nine-Tails.

Key Points:
- The seal splits and contains the beast's chakra; a Four Symbols or
  gate mechanism regulates the flow the host may draw upon.
- A concealed key (stored separately) allows the seal to be loosened or
  reinforced by an authorized master.
- Improper tampering risks weakening the seal and releasing the beast.

Related: the Uzumaki clan of Whirlpool were renowned masters of sealing;
their bloodline is bound up with the maintenance of this seal on Naruto
Uzumaki. See the Nine-Tails containment log. Only certified sealing
masters may inspect or adjust a jinchuriki seal, under Hokage order.
